    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">When warehouses in Selangor outgrow their floorspace, the cheapest expansion is up — adding a mezzanine for inventory storage. The decking material decides whether the project lands within budget or runs over. Plywood works, but it is heavy, expensive, and requires beefier steel frames. Honeycomb cardboard panels — yes, paper-based, but engineered to load-rated specifications — are quietly displacing plywood on light-storage mezzanines across Klang Valley logistics yards. Here is when they make sense and how to spec them.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Where Honeycomb Decking Wins</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Light-Storage Inventory Floors</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">For mezzanines holding cartons of finished goods, slow-moving stock, seasonal inventory, or office storage, honeycomb panels at 30-50mm thickness easily carry 250-500kg/m² distributed load — well above what carton storage actually puts on the floor. The weight saving on the deck itself reduces required steel section sizes by 20-30%, which is where the project cost comes down.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Renovation & Retrofit Projects</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Adding a mezzanine inside an existing warehouse means working around live operations. Honeycomb panels arrive flat, lift in by hand, and install without the noise and dust of plywood saw-cutting on site. Installation is faster and disrupts trading less. Important when your warehouse runs 24/6.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Modular & Temporary Platforms</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Pop-up retail, exhibition raised platforms, event staging, temporary access decks — honeycomb panels assemble and disassemble repeatedly without the weight of plywood. Easier to truck between sites, store flat between events, and dispose cleanly when the structure is decommissioned.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Specification Guide</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Panel Thickness & Load Rating</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">30mm honeycomb sandwich panel — 350kg/m² distributed load with 600mm joist spacing. Suits light carton storage. 50mm honeycomb sandwich panel — 500kg/m² distributed load with 900mm joist spacing. Suits heavier carton storage and walk-traffic mezzanines. For point loads (palletised heavy items), specify 75mm with reinforced steel-flex facing.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Surface Finish</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Standard panels come with smooth kraft facing — sufficient for most applications. For high-foot-traffic platforms, specify the wear-resistant phenolic-faced upgrade — same dimensions, abrasion-rated surface that handles years of footsteps without scuffing through to the honeycomb core.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Fire & Compliance Spec</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Selangor Bomba requires fire-rated decking for commercial warehouse mezzanines. Our fire-retardant treated honeycomb panels carry Class 2 surface spread of flame certification. Always confirm with your project's fire safety officer before installation — the certificate is provided on request.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Installation in Practice</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Panels arrive on pallets, cut to your floor plan dimensions. A two-person team lifts each panel (typically 25-45kg), positions on the steel mezzanine frame, and fastens with self-tapping screws on a 300mm screw centre pattern around the edge plus 600mm centres in the field. No saw cutting on site (we cut the openings for stair voids, lift wells, and column penetrations at our Balakong facility based on your drawings). A 100m² mezzanine decks in a single working day with two people.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="bg-surface-variant/50 border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-8 my-12">
