          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Mezzanine Honeycomb FAQs</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Can honeycomb be used as mezzanine flooring?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Yes — for light-storage mezzanines, 250-500kg/m² distributed. Always engineer-checked.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Honeycomb vs plywood?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">70% lighter at same stiffness. Lower steel cost, faster install, recyclable end-of-life.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">What thickness needed?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">30mm for ≤350kg/m² loads, 50mm for ≤500kg/m². 75mm for point-loaded pallet mezzanines.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Is it fire-rated?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Standard is combustible. Fire-retardant Class 2 variant available for Bomba-compliant projects.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="group border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-4">
            <summary class="font-label font-bold text-on-surface cursor-pointer">Can my own team install it?</summary>
            <p class="font-body text-on-surface text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">Yes. Cut-to-fit at our factory, screws to steel frame on site. 100m² in a day with 2 people.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
